<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore non-oil exports fall 8.8 pct in November.</title>
<headline>Singapore non-oil exports fall 8.8 pct in November.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell a nominal 8.8 percent year-on-year in November to Singapore $7.28 billion after rising 1.1 percent in October, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Friday.</p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports fell 8.3 percent in November to S$8.97 billion after rising 6.9 pct in October.  </p>
<p>Trade in nominal terms, in bln S$ at current prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				  November		   October</p>
<p>Total trade	   30.76 (-1.4)	    32.06 (3.3)</p>
<p>    Exports		 14.87 (-4.1)	    15.70 (4.8)</p>
<p>Domestic exports     8.75 (-4.1)	     9.03 (3.1)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.47 (29.2)	     1.34 (15.9)</p>
<p>Non-oil		  7.28 (-8.8)	     7.68 (1.1)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     6.13 (-4.1)	     6.68 (7.3)</p>
<p>Imports		 15.89 (1.2)	     16.35 (1.8)</p>
<p>Trade in real terms, in blns of S$ at 1990 prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage change given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				November		October</p>
<p>    Total trade	   35.67 (-0.6)	  37.56 (5.0)</p>
<p>    Exports		 17.75 (-4.1)	  19.16 (6.8)</p>
<p>    Domestic exports    10.88 (-6.5)	  11.70 (4.0)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.91 (3.3)	    1.77 (-9.4)</p>
<p>    Non-oil		  8.97 (-8.3)	   9.93 (6.9)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     6.87 (-0.2)	   7.46 (11.4)</p>
<p>    Imports		 17.92 (3.1)	   18.40 (3.2)</p>
</text>
